# e2e-credential-isolation.patch  --  SignalDeck Remediation Round 2, SWARM 2 (finding C3)
#
# TARGET FILES (paths are repo-root relative to  .../claude code/signaldeck )
#   1. daemon/internal/config/config.go            MODIFIED  (projectRoot: explicit root wins, blank fails closed)
#   2. daemon/e2e/e2e_test.go                      MODIFIED  (startDaemon: set SIGNALDECK_ROOT in cmd.Env)
#   3. daemon/internal/config/isolation_test.go    NEW FILE  (proves the leak and the fix)
#
# HOW TO APPLY  --  from the repo root:
#     cd "C:/Users/Nicholas_N/Desktop/claude code/signaldeck"
#     git apply --check round2-drafts/patches/e2e-credential-isolation.patch   # must print nothing
#     git apply         round2-drafts/patches/e2e-credential-isolation.patch
#
# TO VERIFY AFTER APPLYING:
#     cd daemon && go test ./internal/config/ -run 'TestHomeAlone|TestExplicitRoot|TestStatedEmptyRoot' -v
#   Expected: all 3 pass. Reverting only the config.go hunk makes
#   TestExplicitRootNeverReadsTheSurroundingCheckout fail on all three subcases.
#
# WHAT THIS FIXES
#   daemon/e2e/e2e_test.go spawned the daemon with a fake HOME, commented
#   "no .env files -> no Alpaca/LLM keys". That isolation never held.
#   config.projectRoot() probes the WORKING DIRECTORY and walks it upward for an
#   ancestor holding signaldeck/daemon; `go test ./e2e` runs from daemon/e2e
#   INSIDE the real checkout, so the walk returned the real repo root and the
#   spawned daemon read the operator's real daemon/.env (LLM key) and
#   stock-trader/.env (Alpaca keys). The os.UserHomeDir() rung that HOME controls
#   is the LAST resort and was never reached.
#
# NOTE ON THE BRIEF: the brief asked for a NEW override variable
#   (SIGNALDECK_CONFIG_ROOT). One already exists -- SIGNALDECK_ROOT, config.go:34,
#   already the FIRST rung, already honoured before any probing, already
#   non-walking. Adding a second name for the same control would create a
#   precedence question and a second thing to forget. This patch hardens the
#   existing one instead: os.LookupEnv so SET means set, and a blank value fails
#   closed rather than silently falling through to the tree walk.
#
# MISSING .env UNDER AN EXPLICIT ROOT: proceeds with NO credentials, deliberately.
#   Aborting would make an isolated test noisy to run and would push people to
#   unset SIGNALDECK_ROOT to quiet it -- which reopens the exact leak. A blank
#   value is different: it names no root at all, so it panics instead of probing.
#
